    "q-118232": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118232",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the diagrams shows the displacement vector of a person that walks $2$ $\\text{km}$ on a bearing of ${80}^{∘}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We choose an arbitrary point on the plane as the starting point (tail) of the vector. The vertical line shows the north direction.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/604ccf740830c570ee87731a719165cca75d615b3a4c8861d2671ccac95aad2e.png)\n\nWe go ${80}^{∘}$ clockwise from the north. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/c8ba5dcce8a71c4ccea5f4d69a02140c4d0d3a94b1a1b914afd7e7dab0600ed8.png)\n\nThe length of the line segment of the vector represents the displacement of the person (which is $2$ $\\text{km}$).",
