    "q-118246": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118246",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/e919070b5c3a6bb82de164b6718abfb0229b0d899a89b1acabb59b5db5162184.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\text{a}$ and a point $O$ shown above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector that is equal to the vector $\\text{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we sketch the line that is passing through $O$ and parallel to $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/81db9168d76c931c3e127ff8cc5b598627dace90f001508c7591ac3a4110f472.png)\n\nNow, we choose a point $A$ on the line, in the direction of $\\text{a},$ such that $OA$ equals the length of $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/96f67d4b61bd215436d4a975051daa3d7587d3f1d125bae03ca9081a822dc69a.png)\n\nSo, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\text{a}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
