      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/b968f83df851f5b19e7073192d7d65f938440be62c60859f553b33b75c852170.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\text{a}$ and a point $O$ shown above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector that is equal to the vector $\\text{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we sketch the line that is passing through $O$ and parallel to $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/12579c5ee42e21b0a312f628bda36992fc343ace38dfbc2758a2e3d6aed49124.png)\n\nNow, we choose a point $A$ on the line, in the direction of $\\text{a},$ such that $OA$ equals the length of $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/cdda8763ddc663d090099a30731d212a076b24063c7fdfeef9c0f7d9505709e1.png)\n\nSo, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\text{a}.$",
