    "q-69469": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69469",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/f7519503298cbdc42274b534e5cf63afea8e9c41cd21055ca80b2e022c00433d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following is true?",
      "worked_solution": "Two vectors are equal if and only if they lie on parallel lines and have both the same magnitude and the same direction.\n\nThe vectors $c$ and $d$ have opposite directions, hence, $c\\ne d.$ \n\nSo, the only equal vectors are $a=b=e.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/2f8c399cf8c69231e87da94f1903e464f5edb433811a3b743995ceb038fd4421.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
